quantities, measures, and named parts give weaker negatives. Selected
non-partitive complements and idioms give positive estimates. Also handle
numeric '%' and percent-format specifiers such as '%s' and '%d'.
These are coarse lexical rules, not a general grammar: unlisted cases
return zero. Only the current and previous token are used, within a document.
