Recognizable proof-page headings and definition/axiom labels establish
proof context. Dotted leaders mixed with nonbreaking spaces provide a
second cue; styled mathematical letters provide a local mathematical cue.
These contexts strengthen responses to spaces, dotted leaders and logic
symbols. Elsewhere, fixed responses cover arrows and proof words. A few
proof-page field names and theorem/attribution word endings also respond.

